# The rows of Array.from for a call on `Array` take every call: a mapper that is undefined, one that is a function, and one that is neither, for which a TypeError is thrown before anything is touched.
# So more than the reach hangs on them: what a call with a mapper that nobody knows answers is typed by the rows (a list that has just been made), the function of the library behind them may be called
# directly, and behind a mapper that is proven to be neither the call never returns. Each of the three through one function, a mapper that is a closure on one way and a number on the other, and what
# stands behind and around a call that always throws.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# CHECK: true
# CHECK-NEXT: 2,3 1,2
# CHECK-NEXT: 0 TypeError
# CHECK-NEXT: 1 true 2 10,20
# CHECK-NEXT: 2 TypeError
# CHECK-NEXT: 3 true 2 10,20
# CHECK-NEXT: in, caught TypeError, at last
# CHECK-NEXT: touched 0
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# -- source: array-from-with-each-kind-of-mapper.ts
